WEBVTT

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:07.179
Seed, lime and fertilizer all go on the record the same way.

00:00:07.179 --> 00:00:11.190
Start on the map, at the area that was treated, and tap it.

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:15.009
The popup shows what is on file for that area.

00:00:15.009 --> 00:00:16.631
Open Actions, then Edit.

00:00:17.338 --> 00:00:23.105
Scroll down to Applications. One drawing carries as many applications as the work took.

00:00:23.105 --> 00:00:24.828
The first row is the seed.

00:00:25.539 --> 00:00:28.473
Name the mix and enter the rate from the spec.

00:00:28.473 --> 00:00:33.959
GroundLog multiplies the rate by the acres you drew, and shows what the area requires.

00:00:34.659 --> 00:00:38.929
Then enter what actually went down, and how many seed tags you collected.

00:00:39.631 --> 00:00:45.701
Add a row for each amendment. Pick lime, name the product, then set the rate and the unit.

00:00:46.401 --> 00:00:52.521
Then the fertilizer. Every row writes its own note as you go, so nothing is typed twice.

00:00:53.234 --> 00:01:01.634
Save the entry. The tracker log now carries the materials, the rates and the totals, and they flow to the seeding record on their own.
